Okay, well not of all time.  But I just lost a significant amount of my taste
for the game with this one.

A spoiler trap opens beneath you!--More--

You fall onto a set of spoilers.

First character that ever even survived the quest, an archaeologist: I made it
all the way through Medusa, Ft. Ludios, Gehennom, Vlad's Tower, The Wizard's
Tower, found the Vibrating Square (tm), and, having finally found his seventh
candle (there were four in the light shop.  He found another, and found a
shop with another, and then polypiled several times until he could at last
create the necessary 7th), lit the candelabrum, rang the bell, read the book,
and went down to meet the High Priestess of Moloch.

A wand of death was all it took to send the Priestess to meet Moloch
personally, and then it was back up again, fast as I could, switching back
and forth between Excalibur and Vorpy as I ran for maximum effect.  Back
through Gehennom, the Fort, the Dungeons of Doom... piece of cake.  Didn't
even break a sweat.  Went up the staircase... and found the elemental plane
of earth.  Was a little fazed by that one, but, finally figuring out that
+5 Excalibur beat out +0 Vorpy, especially given that earth elemtals _have_
no heads, I cleaned up the level, found the portal, and went on to bigger and
better things.  Or, rather, bigger and _worse_ things.

I met the elemental plane of air.  That hellhole is the most incredibly
annoying place I ever had the misfortune to set foot upon (and I use that
phrase loosely).  I figured out quickly to use my ring of levitation to
move about freely, but that didn't help me find the portal at all.

Buffeted about by air elementals and dragons of all types, I teleported about
in order to keep my hitpoints at a safe level.  And all of a sudden, things
just came to a crashing halt.  I was looking around for that *&(^ portal
(no scrolls of gold detection--couldn't _find_ the cursed things anywyere...)
and my Orb of Detection was perpetually unclear in its visions.  (Just like
Quetzalcoatl was perpetually upset at me for reasons I could not fathom.)
Suddenly, lightning struck from the clouds, destroying my ring of levitation.
Quickly, I snapped on a ring of regeneration (figuring I would need it)--and
then, the Wizard of Yendor showed up.  And summoned 4711 monsters.  Followed
me everywhere I teleported, and _KEPT_ summoning monsters.  I couldn't even
fight back effectively.  I sat back and watched helplessly as my 300 hit
points drained to zero--twice in succession.

I didn't even make the high score list.  The program hit a floating exception
and died.

**SIGH**

I can't even imagine how people who have to fight Archons get through
there...
